# Generated by scripts/tx-tests.mjs from the HL7 FHIR terminology-ecosystem tests
# (https://github.com/HL7/fhir-tx-ecosystem-ig, tests/test-cases.json at main).
# The whole set in one file: 1178 test cases in 38 suites, for a FHIR
# 5.0 server. Do not edit; re-run the generator.
#
# ITB stores one test suite per feature file, so this file is the whole test set
# as a single suite. The per-suite files beside it hold the same tests split 38
# ways; deploy either shape, not both.
#
# Each scenario names the resources its suite depends on, which travel with the
# request as tx-resource parameters. That repeats per test case, which is what
# already happens at run time: a Background runs once per test case too.
@lang:itb-core-en@^2 @dialect:fhir-terminology@^1 @dialect:fhir-validator@^2 @suite:all
Feature: tx-tests-full
  Every test case of the HL7 terminology-ecosystem test set, in the suites the set
  defines: 1178 of them, for a FHIR 5.0 server. A suite whose upstream mode is
  not "general" is expected only of a server that supports that mode.

  Background:
    Given TxServer is the system under test at "https://178.104.103.200.sslip.io/tx/r5"
    And FHIRValidator is a fhir-validator at "http://fhir-validator:8080"
    And Client is infrastructure
    And Client fetches the test material from "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/HL7/fhir-tx-ecosystem-ig/main/tests/"

  # Tests for minimal requirements for metadata statements. These tests apply to all servers
  Rule: metadata

    # Check that the minimum expected things are found in the server CapabilityStatement
    @operation:metadata
    Scenario: metadata
      When Client reads the capability statement of TxServer as $capabilities
      Then $response.status should be 200
      And $capabilities should contain the pattern in "capstmt.json"

    # Check that the minimum expected things are found in the server TerminologyCapabilities
    @operation:term-caps
    Scenario: term-caps
      When Client reads the terminology capabilities of TxServer as $capabilities
      Then $response.status should be 200
      And $capabilities should contain the pattern in "capterms.json"

